WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:13.689
The Operations calendar lays out every store’s day, hour by hour: checklists, deliveries, repairs and tasks, each with the person on it. In this video, you’ll read the day, change the view, and add and move work.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:22.447
Open Operations. Calendar is the first tab, next to Shifts and the Daily brief. Today, there’s a column for each café.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:30.793
Above the grid is the day at a glance: how many tasks, how many are done, open and overdue, and how far along each café is.

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:39.809
Each task sits at its time, with the person on it. Overdue ones are flagged, finished ones get a tick, and every ticket type has its own color.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:47.520
Too much going on? Tap a ticket type to show only that kind of work, like checklists, then tap it again to bring the rest back.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.105
Pick one location at the top to focus on a single café.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:58.305
Then choose Team member, to get a column for each person instead, so you can see who has too much on.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:05.273
Switch to Week to plan ahead, or Month for the bigger picture. The arrows move you along, and Today brings you back.

00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:15.752
To add work, click New task. Pick the location, the ticket type, who’s on it, and the time, and it lands on the calendar.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.552
Already have the ticket? Add existing ticket gives it a time slot instead.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:29.128
Click any task to open it, mark it done, or give it a new time. And Show on TV puts today’s calendar on the screen in the back of house.

